  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/679B0F">Remark <span data-tag="679B0F">1.2.2.5</span>.</a>HomLS@$\Hom ^{\lft }_{S}(X,Y)$ The definition of $\Hom ^{\rght }_{S}(x,y)$ is not self-dual: that is, $\Hom ^{\rght }_{S^{op}}(x,y) \neq \Hom ^{\rght }_{S}(y,x)$ in general. Instead we define $\Hom ^{\lft }_ S(x,y) = \Hom ^{\rght }_{S^{op}}(y,x)^{op}$, so that $\Hom ^{\lft }_{S}(x,y)_ n$ is the set of all $z \in S_{n+1}$ such that $z|\Delta ^{ \{ 0\}  } = x$ and $z | \Delta ^{ \{ 1, \ldots , n+1\}  }$ is the constant simplex at the vertex $y$. </p>
